From: Local OpenWrt build <local@dendelion.invalid>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: ignore unusable S8_MIN country power

A malformed Country element can advertise 0x80 as the maximum transmit
power. The field is signed, so mac80211 interprets this as -128 dBm and the
802.11h calculation clamps it to 0 dBm. On a PHY shared by managed and AP
interfaces, that makes the local AP effectively unusable as well.

Treat only S8_MIN as an invalid channel-power value. Skipping the malformed
triplet leaves the local regulatory maximum in force; valid peer power
constraints and the separate Power Constraint element remain unchanged.

---
 net/mac80211/mlme.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/net/mac80211/mlme.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/mlme.c
@@ -3157,6 +3157,15 @@ ieee80211_find_80211h_pwr_constr(struct
 
 		for (i = 0; i < triplet->chans.num_channels; i++) {
 			if (first_channel + i * chan_increment == chan) {
+				/*
+				 * S8_MIN cannot be a useful transmit-power
+				 * constraint. Applying it would be clamped to
+				 * 0 dBm below and can affect every interface on
+				 * a shared PHY. Ignore only this malformed value
+				 * and continue looking for a valid triplet.
+				 */
+				if (triplet->chans.max_power == S8_MIN)
+					goto next;
 				have_chan_pwr = true;
 				*chan_pwr = triplet->chans.max_power;
 				break;
